Trash values are assign on ArrayRef when using initializer_list on msvc(Release, /O2)
Codes
int main()
{
        uint32_t x = 64;
	c10::ArrayRef<int64_t> a({64, 64, 64, 64});
	std::cout << "a : " << a << std::endl;
	return 0;
}

Results
a : [834242869776, 4, 140734498917936, 0]

Expected behavior
a : [64, 64, 64, 64]

( working on gcc )
Environment
OS: Microsoft Windows 10 Pro
Compiler : Microsoft Visual C++ 2019
Flags : O2  (actually the problem happens on /Og)
Additional context
I think, when msvc optimzation codes, compiler have removed the temporary initializer_list before passed on constructor in this line c10::ArrayRef<int64_t> a({64, 64, 64, 64});
So if under code is working fine
int main()
{
        uint32_t x = 64;
        std::initializer_list<int64_t> y = {64, 64, 64, 64};
	c10::ArrayRef<int64_t> a(y);
	std::cout << "a : " << a << std::endl;
	return 0;
}

